{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages","id":916338,"title":"[Minor Template] Influence-based Mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-17T11:25:11-07:00","id":916338,"title":"[Minor Template] Influence-based Mages","content":"So, I was looking into allowing a minor template access to ephemeral Influences, and bouncing things around trying to balance them. I was also looking at Mage threads. Then it occurred to me (and I doubt I'm at all alone in this), that the Influence models could easily recreate a slimmed down, Mage-like minor template. So how would that look?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Mage (minor template)</b></span><br /> <br /> Some, through dedication, worship, secret knowledge, or gifts, command powers of the world to work their will. These individuals go by many names - witch, mage, shaman, necromancer, theurge - but all are joined by their ability to Influence various forces to fulfill their desires. Through utilizing the spiritual powers of Essence, they can affect some of the same powers and abilities as ghost, spirits, and angels are capable of.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mechanics</b></span><br /> <br /> A Mage character has:<br /> <b>Potency</b> - Trait (or Supernatural Merit) rated 1-5, increases Essence allowed per Turn, Essence Capacity, and up to what level of Influence can Essence costs be reduced to 0. Counts as Supernatural Tolerance, and Rank for abilities.<br /> <b>Essence</b> - How much energy that can be stored to fuel abilities.<br /> <b>Tradition</b> - Determines themes, flavor, and their Principle Influences. Determines their Power and Finesse Attributes used in their abilities?<br /> <b>Influences</b> - Categories of reality through which they can work their magic. See Chronicles of Darkness, pg 130.<br /> <br /> <u>Effects:</u><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">0 - Sense</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 - Strengthen and Weaken</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022 - Manipulate and Scan</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022 - Control and Scry</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 - Create and Destroy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 - Mass/Permanent Create, Mass Destroy, and Excise</span></span><br /> <br /> <u>Duration:</u><br /> 0 - One minute per success. No additional Essence cost.<br /> \u2022 - Ten minutes per success. No additional Essence cost.<br /> \u2022\u2022 - One hour per success. The cost is 1 additional Essence.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 - One day per success. The cost is 2 additional Essence.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 - Permanent. The cost is 2 additional Essence.<br /> <br /> Note: Duration is additive, so Manipulate for 1 hour per Success is a \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Influence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Sense</b>: You </span></span>can sense sources of Essence appropriate for the Influence up to a mile away<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. Cost 0 Essence.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Weaken</b>: </span></span>You can penalize Defense of a loved one, make an emotion weaker, an animal or plant sicklier, or an object more fragile, reducing Health or Structure by Rank/Potency. This Influence can shift the Open Condition to Anchor, Resonant or Infrastructure for its duration. The cost is 1 Essence<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Scan</b>: Roll your Finesse*. You can ask the Storyteller for details relating to the Influence about the subject your are viewing. Costs 1 Essence.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Scry</b>: You can use the Scan effect upon a subject you can Sense (up to one mile, usually). Costs 2 Essence.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Destroy</b>: </span></span>You can remove an anchor, banish an emotion, kill a plant or animal (Roll Power* + Finesse* as a 0L Weapon), or destroy an object. You can remove an Anchor, Infrastructure, or Resonant Condition in a subject for the duration of the Influence. The cost is 4 Essence.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Excise</b>: As Destroy, but it also prevents the subject from entering, being created, or having an effect in the area for the duration. If dealing damage, treat as 0A Weapon.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Mitigation</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence costs can be mitigated in a number of ways, to a minimum determined by Potency (at Potency 1, \u2022 Influence effects can be reduced to 0, \u2022\u2022 effects at Potency 3, and \u2022\u2022\u2022 effects at Potency 5; otherwise the minimum cost is 1).<br /> Principle Influence - (-1)<br /> Resonant Conditions - Resonance (-1), Open (-2), [Hallow?Controlled?] (-3).<br /> Spell (Major decisions pre-planned) - (-1).<br /> Ritual Casting - Minute (-1), Hour (-2).<br /> Special Tools - (-1, but the Resource or Availability cost must be greater than the Influence level).<br /> These can be combined to bring costs down so repeated use doesn't beggar the mage.<br /> <br /> <b>Numina</b><br /> Mages can learn a number of special applications of their powers. If they can justify a use or expression of the Numina through their Influences, let them acquire it (Fire and Blast makes sense, but if they can justify Love and Blast, let them). </span></span>See Chronicles of Darkness, pg 136 for examples.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Manifestations</b><br /> Mages can even alter their own state of being, or those of their immediate surroundings, much like Ephemerals with Manifestation.</span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u>Materialize</u> - Being inherently material, a Mage gets this for free. This Effect has no cost.<br /> <u>Twilight Form</u> (Requires Open Condition) - By spending 3 Essence, the mage can shift their form into Twilight. They suffer from Essence Bleed as per Ephemeral entities, but will instead Materialize if they run out of Essence (this can range from awkward to messy, depending on <i>where</i> they are forced to Materialize).<br /> <u>Reaching</u> - By spending one Essence, the mage applies the Reaching Condition to themselves. The activation roll is penalized by the local Gauntlet Strength. A mage might do this if they want to affect a Spirit on the other side.<br /> <u>Avernian Gateway</u> (Requires Open Condition) - By spending 3 Essence, the mage opens a nearby gateway to the Underworld, and applies the Underworld Gate Condition to the location.<br /> <u>Shadow Gateway</u> (Potency 3+, Requires Open Condition) - By spending Essence equal to Gauntlet Strength, the mage opens a portal to the Shadow that it and other entities may use, applying the Shadow Gate Condition to the location. The activation roll is penalized by the local Gauntlet Strength.<br /> [Might just replace the above two with the more general Realm Gateway Manifestation floating around the forums...]<br /> <u>Image</u> (Requires Anchor, Resonant, or Infrastructure Condition) - By spending 1 Essence, the mage may use their Influence to shape it into an image, or cast an image upon it. The can be reduced to no cost if the Influence is one of their Principle Influences.<br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Fetter</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Requires Open Condition) - By spending 2 Essence, the mage adds the Fettered Condition to themself. Living beings targeted by this Effect contest the roll with Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. If the Effect is successful, living targets gain the Urged Condition. A mage must be capable of Twilight Form to buy Fetter, and must be in Twilight Form to use it. Some mages report that bodily functions (including aging) cease while in Twilight, and that this is one method of a kind of immortality through haunting. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Unfetter</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Requires Fettered Condition) - By spending 1 point of Essence, the mage temporarily suppresses the Fetter Condition for a Scene, allowing them to use other Manifestation Effects or roam in Twilight. When the Scene ends, any Manifestation Effects used during it immediately end. If the mage isn\u2019t back within range of their Fetter (see p. 134) when Unfetter ends, they immediately Materialize. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Possess</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Requires Open Condition) - By spending 3 Essence, the mage gains temporary control over an object, corpse, or creature, applying the Possessed Condition to the subject. Living subjects contest the roll with Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. A mage must be capable of Twilight Form to buy Possess, and must be in Twilight Form to use it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Claim</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Requires Controlled Condition) - By spending 5 Essence, the mage gains permanent control over an object, creature or corpse, applying the Claimed Condition to the subject. Living subjects contest the roll with Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. A mage must be capable of both the Fetter and Possess Manifestations to buy Claim, and the mage must be in Twilight Form to use it. Long term consequences of merging one's self to other objects and beings are the subject of many dark rumors.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Experience Costs:</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"center\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Trait</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Experiences</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Potency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4 per dot</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Principle Influence</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3 per dot</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Other Influence</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4 per dot</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Numina</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Manifestation</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Tradition Template:</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Name</b><br /> Description<br /> <b>Power:</b> Attribute<br /> <b>Finesse:</b> Skill<br /> <b>Example Principle Influences:</b><br /> <b>Essence Recovery Method:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Example Traditions</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Necromancer</b><br /> Necromancers tap into the lore of the dead to seek knowledge and power over things in their mortal life. Many also deal in the trappings and associations of death as well.<br /> <b>Power:</b> Intelligence<br /> <b>Finesse:</b> Occult<br /> <b>Example Principle Influences: </b>Death, Bones, Passions, Blood<br /> <b>Essence Recovery Method:</b> As per Ghosts - being near Anchors (though having none of their own, any Anchor will do), or being remembered (for their power) by the living.<br /> <br /> <b>Street Shaman</b><br /> Spirits are not restricted to the wilds of nature - every place and thing has its own spiritual reflection. Street Shamans deal with the spirits of the city, to make sure they stay in balance, or merely to advance their own goals.<br /> <b>Power:</b> Manipulation<br /> <b>Finesse:</b> Streetwise<br /> <b>Example Principle Influences: </b>Street, Dogs, Crime, Separation<br /> <b>Essence Recovery Method:</b> Street Shamans usually gain Essence by bargaining with Spirits. Spirits are usually predisposed towards those that further their reflections and cause their Resonance Conditions to appear. Most will give a Street Shaman their cut in exchange for such help.<br /> <br /> <b>Machine-Priest</b><br /> Some heed the static hymns only few can hear. Worshiping a divine of infinite clockwork complexity, they further what they believe to be Its tenants - and if sometimes that matches their own desires, who can say?<br /> <b>Power:</b> Wits<br /> <b>Finesse:</b> Persuasion<br /> <b>Example Principle Influences:</b> Machines, Fate, Awe, Order<br /> <b>Essence Recovery Method:</b> As per Angels - being near Infrastructure is the most common method, though some manage to get their congregations/cults to make sacrifices to them to fuel their power.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b><br /> If you want, you can also use @amechra's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/742772-i-ve-got-nobilis-3e-on-my-mind\">Dharmas and Influences</a>.<br /> If you have Mage: the Awakening 2E and want to use this minor template anyways, you can also model them like Ghost Mages (but not, you know, Ghosts). Influences would map to the Arcana, and Numina can be Mage Spells as if they were Praxis. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Examples to follow. Feel free to discuss in the meantime. I'll post more when I have time.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-23-2016, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T12:44:31-07:00","id":916371,"title":"","content":"I've always loved the idea of 'Influence Magic' as a minor template or other sort of character option, but never got around to writing something up.<br /> <br /> Numina might work as a nice way to cover &quot;Spells&quot;, just attach them to an influence level as a prerequisite, so long as the influence is thematically appropriate (Blast can work for nearly anything with a physical manifestation, but might not work with &quot;Love&quot;).<br /> <br /> One idea might be to have the Path (or whatever you call it) correspond to an ephemeral type. Path of the Underworld/Necromancy/Death-Mages/whatever name might focus on ghost and similar based influences, while the Path of the Shadow/Shamanism/etc draw influence similarly to spirits, The Path of the Astral/Warlocks/etc equate to goetics, and Stigmatic-Mages/God-Machine Priests/etc work like Angels. That'd define the manifestation conditions they can interact with for their essence bonuses and replenishment, and would give you a guide for starting Influences.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 06-17-2016, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T13:03:43-07:00","id":916385,"title":"","content":"<b>Example:</b> Pyris<br /> <b>Tradition:</b> Something vaguely Zoroastrian like - Principle Influences: Fire, Truth<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Fire 4, Truth 3, Light 1<br /> <b>Gnosis/Potency/Whatever:</b> 4<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 6/14 (4/turn)<br /> <br /> Given this, Pyris can Create (for a duration dependent upon additional Essence spent, as per Influences), Destroy, Control, Scry upon, Manipulate, Scan, Strengthen, Weaken, and Sense Fire. Say they want to Create a flame from nothing. Create costs 4 Essence. That's steep, but they thankfully have a Spell that creates a bonfire (-1 Essence). They are in a hot area already, so we'll give them Resonant (-1). They can afford to take their time, so they drag it out into a ritual (-1). It now only takes them 1 Essence. If the area was Open to Fire somehow, it would only cost 0 Essence (since Fire is a Principle Influence).<br /> <br /> Talking to another, they can Sense the Truth of their words (Influence: Truth 0+), and by spending a point of Essence, Scan it for additional details. Being flexible (as one should with broad Influences), they can Manipulate that Truth, perhaps making the source (the speaker) divulge more or less, for 2 Essence (unless Mitigation brings the number down).<br /> <br /> Seeking to hide, they Weaken the Light in the area. Unfortunately, since Light isn't a Principle Influence, it is going to cost 1 Essence regardless of Mitigation. If they had Influence: Light 2, they might be able to Manipulate the light into perhaps moving around them, leaving only them in shadow, rather than darkening the entire area.<br /> <br /> <b>Note</b>: These examples are extremely rough and Alpha, and serve solely to give a general idea of what I am talking about above.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T13:08:08-07:00","id":916389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=916371#post916371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always loved the idea of 'Influence Magic' as a minor template or other sort of character option, but never got around to writing something up.<br /> <br /> Numina might work as a nice way to cover &quot;Spells&quot;, just attach them to an influence level as a prerequisite, so long as the influence is thematically appropriate (Blast can work for nearly anything with a physical manifestation, but might not work with &quot;Love&quot;).<br /> <br /> One idea might be to have the Path (or whatever you call it) correspond to an ephemeral type. Path of the Underworld/Necromancy/Death-Mages/whatever name might focus on ghost and similar based influences, while the Path of the Shadow/Shamanism/etc draw influence similarly to spirits, The Path of the Astral/Warlocks/etc equate to goetics, and Stigmatic-Mages/God-Machine Priests/etc work like Angels. That'd define the manifestation conditions they can interact with for their essence bonuses and replenishment, and would give you a guide for starting Influences.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, those work too. My whole goal here is to provide a very bare bones system that others can build what they want on, using only the Core material and a little imagination. Grouping Paths (or whatever) by ephemeral type makes great sense as an example.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Numina (flavored with Influence, as desired) works great for more concrete, reliable abilities.<br /> <br /> Also: Love Blasts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T13:22:28-07:00","id":916394,"title":"","content":"Rather than &quot;mages&quot; you could adapt the mini-template to &quot;street shamans&quot;, more akin to the Shadow than to the Supernal. T<br /> Think about it: The Spirits whom the &quot;street shamans&quot;are allied grant them the use of influences and numinas... in exchange to promote and strengthen their resonance. And suddenly you several goups of them performing feng shui over the city and competing between themselves... while their spirit masters move them like pieces in a chess game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T14:10:39-07:00","id":916412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=916394#post916394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than &quot;mages&quot; you could adapt the mini-template to &quot;street shamans&quot;, more akin to the Shadow than to the Supernal. T<br /> Think about it: The Spirits whom the &quot;street shamans&quot;are allied grant them the use of influences and numinas... in exchange to promote and strengthen their resonance. And suddenly you several goups of them performing feng shui over the city and competing between themselves... while their spirit masters move them like pieces in a chess game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, these actually aren't linked to the Supernal at all. They're Blue Book mages. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> More seriously, the reason I went with &quot;mage&quot; is that it is a more general term. You could certainly do Street Shamans, wielding power given/taken from Spirits. You could also do priests or cultists granted authority and influence by their gods. Or mystics tapping raw elemental forces. Or advanced psychics manipulating raw emotions and concepts. Or...<br /> <br /> I'm still trying to think of how to convert Thaumaturges to 2E. I probably wouldn't quite go this route (at least solely), but some people might want to. The best part is that it only requires the Core book (and anything cooked up here, of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T18:57:11-07:00","id":916544,"title":"","content":"I offer you <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/742772-i-ve-got-nobilis-3e-on-my-mind\">Dharmas and Influences</a>, for some <i>real</i> expanded Influences fun. Just recognize that True Influence and True Dharma are essentially plot devices, and should have a different cost swapped out for the Willpower cost (Quintessence? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Actually, just make it a Willpower dot, have True Influence/Dharma move things to a sympathetic-type range rather than waiving range altogether, and you're all set.<br /> <hr /><br /> Under this set up, Pyris would be able to do the following (assuming Fire Influence, Truth Dharma, and Light Influence):<br /> <br /> \u2022 They can gather general information about local fires, play parlour tricks with flames, talk to those flames, prevent fires from going out, and could summon and control fire. If they wanted to create a fire from nothing, that'd be an Invoke influence - that's just 2 Essence, so a ritual (-1) in an area Open (-1) to fire would be enough to conjure flames in whatever shape they wanted.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Truth is an interesting case - they can detect the truthful, colour things with the essential nature of truthfulness (make something sound more plausible or &quot;correct&quot;), project themselves into a truthful statement (talk about trippy!), or give themselves certain elements of truth. Yeah, the higher rank stuff is<i> weird as hell</i>, but they are practically impossible to lie to and I <i>guess</i> Incarnate would do something similar to Scan? Depends on how you interpret it, I guess.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Light would let them map out the general layout of nearby light, and could gather shadows around themselves by using Demonstrate (among other minor tricks). If they had Light 2, they could use Speak to ask a lightbulb to burn out or something similar.<br /> <br /> If they were willing to pull out the <i>big guns</i>, Pyris can gather information on fire pretty much anywhere, could make fire flare a little bit at the sound of their name, or could learn the truth of a situation by looking at any of the component parts.<br /> <br /> If you were to, say, swap out that Light Influence for a Light Dharma? That control over Light becomes much more... metaphorical. Maybe they could detect vampires by seeing their aversion to the light, and they could make moods brighter or otherwise make things more like Light.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T19:35:59-07:00","id":917104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=916544#post916544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I offer you <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/742772-i-ve-got-nobilis-3e-on-my-mind\">Dharmas and Influences</a>, for some <i>real</i> expanded Influences fun. Just recognize that True Influence and True Dharma are essentially plot devices, and should have a different cost swapped out for the Willpower cost (Quintessence? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Actually, just make it a Willpower dot, have True Influence/Dharma move things to a sympathetic-type range rather than waiving range altogether, and you're all set.<br /> <hr /><br /> Under this set up, Pyris would be able to do the following (assuming Fire Influence, Truth Dharma, and Light Influence):<br /> <br /> \u2022 They can gather general information about local fires, play parlour tricks with flames, talk to those flames, prevent fires from going out, and could summon and control fire. If they wanted to create a fire from nothing, that'd be an Invoke influence - that's just 2 Essence, so a ritual (-1) in an area Open (-1) to fire would be enough to conjure flames in whatever shape they wanted.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Truth is an interesting case - they can detect the truthful, colour things with the essential nature of truthfulness (make something sound more plausible or &quot;correct&quot;), project themselves into a truthful statement (talk about trippy!), or give themselves certain elements of truth. Yeah, the higher rank stuff is<i> weird as hell</i>, but they are practically impossible to lie to and I <i>guess</i> Incarnate would do something similar to Scan? Depends on how you interpret it, I guess.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Light would let them map out the general layout of nearby light, and could gather shadows around themselves by using Demonstrate (among other minor tricks). If they had Light 2, they could use Speak to ask a lightbulb to burn out or something similar.<br /> <br /> If they were willing to pull out the <i>big guns</i>, Pyris can gather information on fire pretty much anywhere, could make fire flare a little bit at the sound of their name, or could learn the truth of a situation by looking at any of the component parts.<br /> <br /> If you were to, say, swap out that Light Influence for a Light Dharma? That control over Light becomes much more... metaphorical. Maybe they could detect vampires by seeing their aversion to the light, and they could make moods brighter or otherwise make things more like Light.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting. And excellent, as most of your material is. If someone want to use those, I'd say they can. The only reason I'm not (likely) going to adopt them here is to reduce the amount of stuff someone needs to keep track of from non-Core sources. Ideally, it's &quot;Want a Mage(-light)? Just slap some ephemeral entity stuff on them with these caveats and go.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T02:11:21-07:00","id":917252,"title":"","content":"As you may or may not remember, there's a bit in Second Sight about a thaumaturge finding a ritual to become a spirit.<br /> <br /> So I couldn't help but think of that and see these guys as those who are slowly transforming themselves so that when they die they become spirits. I could just see it. &quot;Oh, my mentor was assassinated last Friday, we have a pool going for when he notices, he always was a space case.&quot; <br /> <br /> Perhaps an optional expansion for mages who are attuned to different forms of essence like spiritual, goetic, angelic, ghostly, which mostly I think would help for crossovers- lucid dreamers for Beast, necromancers for Geist, scientist-sorcerers for Demon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T06:43:00-07:00","id":917317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=917252#post917252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As you may or may not remember, there's a bit in Second Sight about a thaumaturge finding a ritual to become a spirit.<br /> <br /> So I couldn't help but think of that and see these guys as those who are slowly transforming themselves so that when they die they become spirits. I could just see it. &quot;Oh, my mentor was assassinated last Friday, we have a pool going for when he notices, he always was a space case.&quot;<br /> <br /> Perhaps an optional expansion for mages who are attuned to different forms of essence like spiritual, goetic, angelic, ghostly, which mostly I think would help for crossovers- lucid dreamers for Beast, necromancers for Geist, scientist-sorcerers for Demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;shrug&gt; Sure. Transition would be easy. Add a Ban, Bane, and switch Potency for Rank. Assign Attributes to Power, Finesse, and Resistance as needed. Might need to trim some of the Influences, Numina, and Manifestations, though. I figured hard caps would just get in the way here, so there aren't any - an experienced enough &quot;mage&quot; could have a vast number of Influences, Numina, and Manifestations.<br /> <br /> As far as &quot;forms&quot; or frequencies of Essence, I'd assume a &quot;mage&quot; takes what they can get, but specialization is fine too. If you wanted to categorize them by ephemera (and thus, what &quot;frequency&quot; they inhabit if/when they use Twilight Form), that's easy enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-19-2016, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T12:08:12-07:00","id":918730,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> I added a note in the main post linking to your Dharma's and Influences thread as an option.<br /> <br /> Questions to all:<br /> <br /> Any ideas on some suggestions for these &quot;mages&quot; regaining Essence?<br /> <br /> Any idea on what the XP costs should be for these to improve/buy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-21-2016, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T12:44:25-07:00","id":918749,"title":"","content":"For Essence, I think Loci are an easy fit, same as Hallows for normal mages, a place of power to compete over and regain essence at like everyone else with Essence. Beyond that, maybe X times per day they can draw from a resonant (r similar) condition that fits one of their influences and gain essence equal to a Composure + Wits (meditation) roll. And maybe allow them to trade for it by bargaining or strong-arming ephemeral entities.<br /> <br /> As for XP, I'd say probably 3 Experience per dot for the primary/art/etc influences, 4 otherwise, one step below arcana. Makes them about the same cost as disciplines, despite greater utility, but on the other hand disciplines tend to be more powerful 1 to 1 than Influences. <br /> <br /> For Numina, I'd suggest 1 Experience if they can already pull off the effect with their Influences (like if they have Influence (Fire) 4 but take Blast anyway), and 2 if they have an appropriate Influence but not high enough to mimic the Numina. Sanctity of Numina would effectively make it so it costs 1 less Experience to gain the Influence level needed for a Numina effect you have, maybe? <br /> Manifestations I'd suggest cost a full 3 Experiences, as they're pretty potent to have access to. I'd suggest limiting Manifestation amount by Potency too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:28:19-07:00","id":918774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=918749#post918749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Essence, I think Loci are an easy fit, same as Hallows for normal mages, a place of power to compete over and regain essence at like everyone else with Essence. Beyond that, maybe X times per day they can draw from a resonant (r similar) condition that fits one of their influences and gain essence equal to a Composure + Wits (meditation) roll. And maybe allow them to trade for it by bargaining or strong-arming ephemeral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loci sounds good. Are those listed in Core? (I'll check and edit when I can).<br /> <br /> As for Conditions, what about them being able to &quot;consume&quot; the relevant Condition for 1 Essence? Since with decent Mitigation, they can Create such Conditions at high enough influences, I wouldn't want them to be able &quot;cheat&quot; by Creating a Condition, then mining it for more Essence than they put into it. With Mitigation, they can Create a Condition for 1 Essence, then &quot;recycle&quot; it for a return of 1 Essence. Zero sum. For actually gaining Essence, seek out &quot;natural&quot; sources to harvest. This has the side effect of adding friction with other ephemerals (since they are competing for the same food supply). Positive or Negative?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=918749#post918749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for XP, I'd say probably 3 Experience per dot for the primary/art/etc influences, 4 otherwise, one step below arcana. Makes them about the same cost as disciplines, despite greater utility, but on the other hand disciplines tend to be more powerful 1 to 1 than Influences.<br /> <br /> For Numina, I'd suggest 1 Experience if they can already pull off the effect with their Influences (like if they have Influence (Fire) 4 but take Blast anyway), and 2 if they have an appropriate Influence but not high enough to mimic the Numina. Sanctity of Numina would effectively make it so it costs 1 less Experience to gain the Influence level needed for a Numina effect you have, maybe?<br /> Manifestations I'd suggest cost a full 3 Experiences, as they're pretty potent to have access to. I'd suggest limiting Manifestation amount by Potency too.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"center\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Trait</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Experiences</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Principle Influence</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3 per dot</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Other Influence</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4 per dot</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Appropriate Numina*</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Other Numina</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Manifestation</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> </tr> </table></div> * = Appropriate Numina are those that could be replicated through Influences. If the Mage ever becomes capable of doing so, refund 1 XP. If they ever lose the ability to replicate a Numina effect through their Influences, have them pay 1 XP (or go into XP debt).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:35:28-07:00","id":918784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=918774#post918774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Loci sounds good. Are those listed in Core? (I'll check and edit when I can).<br /> <br /> As for Conditions, what about them being able to &quot;consume&quot; the relevant Condition for 1 Essence? Since with decent Mitigation, they can Create such Conditions at high enough influences, I wouldn't want them to be able &quot;cheat&quot; by Creating a Condition, then mining it for more Essence than they put into it. With Mitigation, they can Create a Condition for 1 Essence, then &quot;recycle&quot; it for a return of 1 Essence. Zero sum. For actually gaining Essence, seek out &quot;natural&quot; sources to harvest. This has the side effect of adding friction with other ephemerals (since they are competing for the same food supply). Positive or Negative?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the sound of that, it makes sense. I believe Loci are mentioned in the core on a basic level, but I don't have my own book open in front of me either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"center\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Trait</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Experiences</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Principle Influence</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3 per dot</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Other Influence</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4 per dot</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Appropriate Numina*</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Other Numina</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Manifestation</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> </tr> </table></div> * = Appropriate Numina are those that could be replicated through Influences. If the Mage ever becomes capable of doing so, refund 1 XP. If they ever lose the ability to replicate a Numina effect through their Influences, have them pay 1 XP (or go into XP debt). </div> </div> </div>Also looks good!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T14:25:14-07:00","id":918803,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on the Tradition/Path/Art defined Power and Finesse stats? Just pick the relevant Attributes? Make one an Attribute and one a Skill?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T14:36:53-07:00","id":918806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=918803#post918803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts on the Tradition/Path/Art defined Power and Finesse stats? Just pick the relevant Attributes? Make one an Attribute and one a Skill?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd suggest it needn't be Power/Finesse, have it be something like a choice of 2 attributes for the Tradition, and then add it to a skill that relates to the influence, kinda like how you can choose any skill that makes sense for Rotes in mage. So, Love might use Persuasion, Empathy, or Socialize, but Fire might use Intimidation, Occult, or Survival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T14:49:37-07:00","id":918812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=918806#post918806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd suggest it needn't be Power/Finesse, have it be something like a choice of 2 attributes for the Tradition, and then add it to a skill that relates to the influence, kinda like how you can choose any skill that makes sense for Rotes in mage. So, Love might use Persuasion, Empathy, or Socialize, but Fire might use Intimidation, Occult, or Survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, roll 3 traits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T15:13:55-07:00","id":918833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=918812#post918812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, roll 3 traits?</div> </div> </div> </div>No I meant, you have two to choose from and use the higher, for attribute","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T19:48:48-07:00","id":918920,"title":"","content":"Ideas for mages regaining essence-<br /> <br /> Having a lair/workshop, just like an ephemeral can gain one essence a day from being near infrastructure/anchor/being near the thing they embody.<br /> <br /> Perhaps they can choose an influence and that becomes their resonance- so a fire mage can regain essence near fires, a technomancer gains essence around machinery, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Willpower- Perhaps when fulfilling their virtue or vice (perhaps it's a choice of which, right hand path versus left hand path sort of thing), they can instead of refilling willpower gain essence.<br /> <br /> If you don't mind more predatory mages<br /> <br /> Well there's always the old standby of consuming an ephemeral for their essence, although it would take a powerful mage to make a habit out of that<br /> <br /> Or sacrifices like an angel- destroying an item ritually gives as much essence as its resource cost, human sacrifices give off as much as the victims integrity.<br /> <br /> A more faustian angle is to have mages earn essence from ephemerals- helping a ghost do it's unfinished business, help a spirit expand its influence in the real world, helping an angel do its mission.<br /> <br /> In the book of spirits, there's a flaw and a merit in which spilling ones own blood produces essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 06-21-2016, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T07:34:11-07:00","id":919084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=918920#post918920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas for mages regaining essence-<br /> <br /> Having a lair/workshop, just like an ephemeral can gain one essence a day from being near infrastructure/anchor/being near the thing they embody.<br /> <br /> Perhaps they can choose an influence and that becomes their resonance- so a fire mage can regain essence near fires, a technomancer gains essence around machinery, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Willpower- Perhaps when fulfilling their virtue or vice (perhaps it's a choice of which, right hand path versus left hand path sort of thing), they can instead of refilling willpower gain essence.<br /> <br /> If you don't mind more predatory mages<br /> <br /> Well there's always the old standby of consuming an ephemeral for their essence, although it would take a powerful mage to make a habit out of that<br /> <br /> Or sacrifices like an angel- destroying an item ritually gives as much essence as its resource cost, human sacrifices give off as much as the victims integrity.<br /> <br /> A more faustian angle is to have mages earn essence from ephemerals- helping a ghost do it's unfinished business, help a spirit expand its influence in the real world, helping an angel do its mission.<br /> <br /> In the book of spirits, there's a flaw and a merit in which spilling ones own blood produces essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the above?<br /> <br /> I'd say, a mage can pick one that fits, or have access to all of them as their inclinations fit. Maybe restrict it by Tradition/Path/Art? Or make such restrictions an potential Drawback option? Like Necromancers must replenish Essence like a Ghost (stay near an Anchor, or make sure others &quot;remember&quot; them, such as by terrorizing the countryside).<br /> <br /> Regarding Influences and Conditions, maybe they can tap one such Condition per day, per Influence? Diversifying leads to greater potential Fuel as the cost of actual depth to their power (5 Influences at 1 leads to a lot of refueling, but weak powers, while 1 Influence at 5 is limited in refueling, but has great power).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T08:14:16-07:00","id":919096,"title":"","content":"I think in regards to pricing these things, it is worth mentioning that <b>The Pack </b>priced out Numina and Influences for the first time. A Numen is 4XP and an Influence dot is 5XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T10:49:20-07:00","id":919194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=919096#post919096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in regards to pricing these things, it is worth mentioning that <b>The Pack </b>priced out Numina and Influences for the first time. A Numen is 4XP and an Influence dot is 5XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll update to use that, then. It seems about right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T10:54:10-07:00","id":919199,"title":"","content":"ISn't that for totems, though, or am I misremembering what that's for? I think those are both a little high for the intent of this template, since you can't have 5 different people and a dozen wolf bloods contributing to get you XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T10:57:11-07:00","id":919201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=919199#post919199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ISn't that for totems, though, or am I misremembering what that's for? I think those are both a little high for the intent of this template, since you can't have 5 different people and a dozen wolf bloods contributing to get you XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. But Disciplines and Arcana cost about the same (a little less, granted, but Influences and Numina are usually scaled for NPCs).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T10:59:13-07:00","id":919202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=919201#post919201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe. But Disciplines and Arcana cost about the same (a little less, granted, but Influences and Numina are usually scaled for NPCs).</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, that's what I mean, they're scaled for NPCs, when they're meant for a PC's main power source they should probably be a bit cheaper. At the very least both should still have the cost break for a duplicatable numina and an affinity influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T11:12:27-07:00","id":919211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=919202#post919202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, that's what I mean, they're scaled for NPCs, when they're meant for a PC's main power source they should probably be a bit cheaper. At the very least both should still have the cost break for a duplicatable numina and an affinity influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be throwing a bit much on Tradition/Path/Art/Paradigm's (any ideas on a final name for this, people?) plate, but I suppose affinity Numina might be under there too (Blast might fit more martial or destructive traditions more than one dedicated towards learning or healing, for instance).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T12:14:17-07:00","id":919247,"title":"","content":"My gut says 2xp/3xp - and my gut does all my math, so I trust those numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T14:49:37-07:00","id":919328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=919247#post919247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My gut says 2xp/3xp - and my gut does all my math, so I trust those numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that like off loading processing to the GPU?<br /> <br /> 2XP/3XP for Numina or Influence dots? Or is that Numina/Influence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T18:00:18-07:00","id":919416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=919328#post919328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that like off loading processing to the GPU?<br /> <br /> 2XP/3XP for Numina or Influence dots? Or is that Numina/Influence?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more like I have a black box in my head where information goes in and information comes out. My subconscious is a <i>beast</i>.<br /> <br /> More on topic, the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T12:56:25-07:00","id":919882,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts regarding something like a &quot;Transform&quot; Influence Effect, where upon you can shift something from one Influence into another you possess?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:27:42-07:00","id":919909,"title":"","content":"Dharma (Foo) 5 (Strip) and Dharma (Bar) 4 (Enchant).<br /> <br /> You take the property of being &quot;foo&quot; away, and then you instil the property of being &quot;bar&quot;.<br /> <br /> More seriously, the edge-cases are <i>staggering</i>. What does it <i>mean</i> when you transform a tree into happiness? Or the colour blue into singing? How do you decide how things shift through layers of abstraction? What about stuff on different <i>mechanical</i> layers? What are the <i>limits</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:45:50-07:00","id":919924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=919909#post919909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dharma (Foo) 5 (Strip) and Dharma (Bar) 4 (Enchant).<br /> <br /> You take the property of being &quot;foo&quot; away, and then you instil the property of being &quot;bar&quot;.<br /> <br /> More seriously, the edge-cases are <i>staggering</i>. What does it <i>mean</i> when you transform a tree into happiness? Or the colour blue into singing? How do you decide how things shift through layers of abstraction? What about stuff on different <i>mechanical</i> layers? What are the <i>limits</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I can see a few ways to handle it.<br /> <br /> 1. If using Dharmas, only allow transforms from Dharma to Dharma and Influence to Influence. Or just Abstract to Abstract and Concrete to Concrete. Like to like.<br /> 2. Only let you transform the Condition part of things. So you switch that Tree Resonance with Happiness Resonance (making any Joy Spirits that show up very confused).<br /> 3. Ban uses that can't be properly explained. If you (temporarily, unless you can make it permanent) transform a tree into happiness, maybe everyone in the area becomes happy, until the Influence expires, and the tree returns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T15:05:02-07:00","id":919967,"title":"","content":"I'd say you'd need 4 dots to turn one thing into another, influence-wise. You essentially need to destroy it in one form and recreate it in another, since there's no equivalent of Patterning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T18:45:23-07:00","id":921802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=919967#post919967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say you'd need 4 dots to turn one thing into another, influence-wise. You essentially need to destroy it in one form and recreate it in another, since there's no equivalent of Patterning.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that's what I was thinking. But changing something else that exists should be easier than creating it ex nihilo. Right? Maybe just discount the &quot;transform&quot; action in Essence and time (like, it has a base of 4 Essence and 1 Action, not the 8 Essence and 2 Actions it would take to do a proper Destroy followed by Create)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T00:08:24-07:00","id":921878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=921802#post921802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, that's what I was thinking. But changing something else that exists should be easier than creating it ex nihilo. Right? Maybe just discount the &quot;transform&quot; action in Essence and time (like, it has a base of 4 Essence and 1 Action, not the 8 Essence and 2 Actions it would take to do a proper Destroy followed by Create)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a discount based on it being only one instead of two uses makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T13:35:31-07:00","id":924590,"title":"","content":"Anyone else have any ideas, or is this good as is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T12:29:59-07:00","id":924982,"title":"","content":"Well I had a few thoughts-<br /> <br /> Should these guys have honorary ephemeral rank like werewolves and one would expect 2d edition sin-eaters to have? <br /> <br /> I was also wondering how specific were you folks imagining their influences to be? Influences can range from as broad as the 10 arcana of mage to extremely specific. And if do allow influences to range from the broad to the specific, have you considered giving advantages to specialists? <br /> <br /> Perhaps specialty dice, or treat specialization like a flaw so that if the lack of magical generalization causes a problem they gain a beat? Not that it necessarily needs a bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T17:18:46-07:00","id":925120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=924982#post924982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well I had a few thoughts-<br /> <br /> Should these guys have honorary ephemeral rank like werewolves and one would expect 2d edition sin-eaters to have? <br /> <br /> I was also wondering how specific were you folks imagining their influences to be? Influences can range from as broad as the 10 arcana of mage to extremely specific. And if do allow influences to range from the broad to the specific, have you considered giving advantages to specialists? <br /> <br /> Perhaps specialty dice, or treat specialization like a flaw so that if the lack of magical generalization causes a problem they gain a beat? Not that it necessarily needs a bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my internal doc, I actually have a merit thst grants Honorary Rank. Rated 3-5, you spend Essence to get that much Rank for a Scene. One version per Ephemeral. <br /> <br /> I'm inclined to let it be as general/specific as a group wants. If you wanted to post a suggestion on how to handle it, that would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T02:08:11-07:00","id":925275,"title":"","content":"Well I didn't have a graph or anything, but as a rule of thumb-<br /> <br /> If you go for the flaw route, how specific it is really doesn't matter, since flaws aren't rated, if say a lust witch gets handicapped in the story because they couldn't manipulate another emotion or even another sin, or even manipulate another mental process, they'd get a beat. <br /> <br /> If one goes this route, one might allow an influence mage to broaden their powers, using the lust witch as an example, perhaps after some studying they could replace that influence- lust, with influence-sin, or influence- emotion, possibly even influence-minds if that's on the table.<br /> <br /> The other option is to give specialization dice, I can see two routes here.<br /> <br /> One, give a number of bonus dice based on how specialized the influence is, in this case mages can trade versatility for raw power.<br /> <br /> If that seems like too much, perhaps make a merit available to those with more specialized influences, perhaps it gives specialty dice, or perhaps it lowers essence costs, I don't know. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T02:35:21-07:00","id":925280,"title":"","content":"Maybe becoming a influence mage involves signing up with one of the spirit Chorus. It is similar to join a gang: you gain the benefits of membership (in this case the associated influences) and a lot of enemies from rival gangs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 07-03-2016, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T02:40:17-07:00","id":925282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=925120#post925120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my internal doc, I actually have a merit thst grants Honorary Rank. Rated 3-5, you spend Essence to get that much Rank for a Scene. One version per Ephemeral.<br /> <br /> I'm inclined to let it be as general/specific as a group wants. If you wanted to post a suggestion on how to handle it, that would be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it should only last a scene, I think honorary rank merits should just give you the rank, similar to Status, but probably more expensive (2 dots per rank, with 5 dots giving you rank 3).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T03:47:39-07:00","id":925291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=925282#post925282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it should only last a scene, I think honorary rank merits should just give you the rank, similar to Status, but probably more expensive (2 dots per rank, with 5 dots giving you rank 3).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you are getting automatic Aggravated damage and potential other social benefits.<br /> <br /> What about make the &quot;Rank&quot; merit simply let you use Status with ephemerals as Honorary Rank?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-03-2016, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:06:06-07:00","id":925566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=925291#post925291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you are getting automatic Aggravated damage and potential other social benefits.<br /> <br /> What about make the &quot;Rank&quot; merit simply let you use Status with ephemerals as Honorary Rank?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only when you're two ranks above them, though, meaning never before rank 3. Meaning a 5 dot merit to do aggravated damage to rank 1 entities of the appropriate type. That seems reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T18:52:21-07:00","id":1082867,"title":"","content":"Would making everything here a flat cost 2Xp per dot be enough to update this to 2e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T19:52:57-07:00","id":1082878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages?p=1082867#post1082867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would making everything here a flat cost 2Xp per dot be enough to update this to 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd bump Potency to 5xp, and drop Influences to 3 and 4 XP, flat. Maybe 2xp and 3xp if you are using more restrictive Influences.<br /> <br /> The others should be fine. Numina still need justification, and Manifestations still require Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[